{"id": "EUVD-2026-76871", "enisaUuid": "1a88cc73-bfc7-3331-8663-49c7abce7efc", "description": "vLLM before 0.28.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability in the LlavaOnevision2 processor loader that ignores the trust_remote_code parameter when loading remote processor classes. Attackers can craft a malicious model with arbitrary code in processing_llava_onevision2.py that executes with vLLM process authority even when trust_remote_code is set to False.", "datePublished": "2026-09-12T12:08:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T18:25:36", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories/GHSA-3c86-2m5g-59q7", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-before-0.28.0-remote-code-execution-via-llavaonevision2-processor"], "aliases": ["PYSEC-2026-3985", "GHSA-rp86-qf3f-pqfc", "CVE-2026-90553"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3c8cd513-3090-3b34-b9f7-ff34976dd966", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.28.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9cc22bf0-334f-394b-a42d-9faa79cb060f", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}